From 0e23176573dac2aed92769b0f4dbdb27dfbf99b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 19:20:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07703/11362] [outer-loop] ARC perception detectors real-frame
 validated: HUD 3/3 confusers, mover 2/2 navigate games (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5833)

The real-frame gate exposed that the first HUD statistic (monotone non-background
count) missed every real counter -- ARC counters change cell VALUES, not fg/bg count
(tu93/bp35 row63 changed on 100% of actions with net count 0). Replaced with
change-fraction + position-independence; added a mover area guard.

Real-frame result (offline arcade, no LLM): HUD recovered on 3/3 confuser games
(bp35 row63, lf52 row0, tu93 row63 -- the exact bars the model mistook for the goal),
mover recovered on 2/2 navigate games (sc25, ls20 color-9 avatar). Honest residuals:
cn04 scattered-color mover FP, sc25 partial-rate meter, r11l/ft09 under-exploration.

9 unit tests + ruff + mypy still clean. Next: fix residuals, then the end-to-end gate
(goal recovery under detector-produced perception).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
